  "notes": "The writerly, harmonically-curious pole of modern country and its most explicit pop/disco crossover — \"acoustic instruments such as pedal steel and banjo with synthesizers and vocoders.\" The harmony is the widest vocabulary in the section and every family here is named in the entry: \"I–V–vi–IV and I–IV–V on the country cuts, ii–V–I and Imaj7–IV on the yacht-rock cuts, i–VII–VI on the minor ones, plus documented 'hazy psychedelia' and disco influence that brings sustained major-7 and add9 voicings into a genre that normally avoids them\" — so the seventh and ninth shares are the highest of any country-pop model here, and the Imaj7–IV pair is authored as I–IV with that extension weighting rather than as a quality-bearing numeral the parser cannot read. The research documents three drum grammars; two are genuinely different lanes and are authored as moods — \"(a) sparse acoustic country with brushes/cross-stick and shaker\" and \"(b) a disco/four-on-the-floor kick with 8th open hats and claps on the crossover cut\" — while (c), the programmed Elektron bed under live cymbals, is a texture rather than a groove and is folded into the base model. The one explicit engine instruction is followed literally: \"model low velocity variance and high shaker/tambourine presence.\" Melody is \"mid-alto, deliberately plain and speech-adjacent with small intervals, long rests, and a conversational rhythm; harmony vocals are self-stacked in unison-plus-octave rather than thirds\" — which is why the counter is an octave echo rather than a lick trade. The mood bands come from the entry's own three sub-bands rather than from the outer 74–130: the `disco crossover` mood is the documented \"2018 crossover 89–120,\" which is why it stops at 120 and not at the base model's 130 — the only 130 reading in the entry is \"'Rainbow' E♭ ~130,\" a piano ballad rather than a disco cut, so it belongs to the base band alone. ⚠ INFERRED: that mood's 118 centre is a choice, not a quote — it sits between the two named crossover readings, \"'Space Cowboy' D♭ ~117\" and \"'High Horse' B minor ~120.\" ⚠ The bass is stated as \"live electric bass mostly … no trap sub,\" so no `drums.bass808` block is authored. ⚠ The per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the mood weights, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
